ing  for ukrainian forces  across the border in the neighboring  russian region of briansk returning  paratroopers are given a hero's welcome  instead of pulling forces back from the  fighting as moscow has previously  announced western observers suspect  russia might simply be rotating units  and preparing for a new phase in this  war  rob mcbride al-jazeera leve  let's get an update with imran khan  who's joining us from the ukrainian  capital akiv imran over to you  two very big explosions in the last four  hours the first one took place around  four o'clock local happened not too far  away from here and then one again about  an hour ago uh both in the same area  those explosions took place uh in the  center of kiev that's the first time  certainly since i've been reporting uh  that um artillery or missiles or rockets  we're not entirely sure what type of  ordinance was used has come this close  to the city center now this all comes  after the russians on tuesday said they  were going to relieve the pressure on  kiev because they understood that there  were decision makers in place by  decision makers they mean the government  frankly so the fact that this has now  happened and it happened twice in the  space of a few hours is very  disconcerting for many we don't know  what building has been hit there's lots  of speculation on social media but the  fact that we weren't allowed to go uh to  the site of the explosion which we have  been able to do in the past suggests  that it's a sensitive location but  uh this all comes like i say um as the  ukrainians are very worried about what  the russians are actually up to and this  has been backed up by the nato secretary  general ian stoltenberg who's actually  said uh a withdrawal is taking place  from key but  he sees it as much more as a  repositioning a regrouping and perhaps  even a resupply for a new phase of the  war whether that comes to kiev or  whether they're going to concentrate  in the east and in the donbas